se-induced gallbladder spasm: less likely due to hemodynamic instability and systemic signs", "Alcoholic hepatitis: inconsistent with acute pain exacerbation during exercise", "Pregnancy-related hyperemesis: less likely given RUQ localization and hypotension"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension with tachycardia (shock suspicion)", "Acute hemodynamic decompensation"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic Emergency with Hemodynamic Instability", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5113636363636366, "posterior": 0.3996192366463619, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The β-hCG test being ordered provides minimal support for a gynecologic emergency (B1) due to pregnancy considerations, but the lack of typical signs like vagi…"], "evidence_against": ["Lack of gynecologic signs (vaginal bleeding, adnexal tenderness) weakly contradicts B1 as the primary cause of acute RUQ pain and shock."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Biliary Tract Obstruction with Hemodynamic Instability", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.22727272727272735, "posterior": 0.07067652689093223, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Exercise-induced RUQ pain weakly supports biliary tract obstruction (B2) as a potential cause, but hemodynamic instability is atypical for this condition."], "evidence_against": ["Chronic alcohol use and rapid weight loss weakly argue against biliary tract obstruction (B2) as the primary cause of symptoms."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine":